  <widget class="QLabel" name="label_maxTile">
   <property name="geometry"><rect><x>490</x><y>34</y><width>150</width><height>16</height></rect></property>
   <property name="text"><string>Max tile cloud cover</string></property>
  </widget>
  <widget class="QLabel" name="icon_maxTile">
   <property name="geometry"><rect><x>645</x><y>34</y><width>16</width><height>16</height></rect></property>
   <property name="font"><font><bold>true</bold></font></property>
   <property name="styleSheet"><string>color: #0066cc;</string></property>
   <property name="text"><string>ⓘ</string></property>
   <property name="toolTip">
    <string>The maximum whole-tile cloud cover (%) a scene may have, per its catalog metadata, to even be considered a candidate. This is a coarse pre-filter applied before your area of interest is looked at.

Example: 30 only considers scenes officially reported as ≤30% cloudy across the ENTIRE tile. Set to 100 to accept any tile and let "Max AOI cloud tolerance" below do the real filtering for your specific area.</string>
   </property>
  </widget>
  <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEdit_maxCloudTile">
   <property name="geometry"><rect><x>490</x><y>54</y><width>100</width><height>22</height></rect></property>
   <property name="text"><string>100</string></property>
  </widget>
  <widget class="QLabel" name="label_maxTol">
   <property name="geometry"><rect><x>490</x><y>84</y><width>160</width><height>16</height></rect></property>
   <property name="text"><string>Max AOI cloud tolerance</string></property>
  </widget>
  <widget class="QLabel" name="icon_maxTol">
   <property name="geometry"><rect><x>655</x><y>84</y><width>16</width><height>16</height></rect></property>
   <property name="font"><font><bold>true</bold></font></property>
   <property name="styleSheet"><string>color: #0066cc;</string></property>
   <property name="text"><string>ⓘ</string></property>
   <property name="toolTip">
    <string>The maximum cloud/shadow cover (%) allowed WITHIN your actual area of interest, measured pixel-by-pixel after download analysis — not the whole tile. If exceeded, the download is skipped (a report is still written explaining why).

Example: 20 skips a scene if more than 20% of your AOI is covered by cloud or shadow, even if the tile overall looked mostly clear.</string>
   </property>
  </widget>
  <widget class="QLineEdit" name="lineEdit_maxCloudTol">
   <property name="geometry"><rect><x>490</x><y>104</y><width>100</width><height>22</height></rect></property>
   <property name="text"><string>20</string></property>
  </widget>

